     "page": 1,
     "text": "Page 28  ##\n**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Harris Alvarez and James Clinic**\n\nPatient: Taylor Mata DOB: 11/11/2004 Sex: F MRN: 405588\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n**2024-12-21** - Visit Reason: Back Strain\n- **BP:** 127/87 mmHg\n- **Weight:** 142 lbs\n\n**2023-10-20** - Visit Reason: ADHD\n- **BP:** 123/85 mmHg\n- **Weight:** 1S3 lbs\n\n**2022-08-18** - Visit Reason: ADHD\n- **BP:** 121/77 mmHg\n- **Weight:** 149 lbs\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n• **ADHD**: Taylor's ADHD has been managed effectively, and she is currently in a controlled phase. She has been prescribed guanfacine 1 mg daily, which has been well-tolerated. The medication has helped in managing her symptoms without significant side effects. \n\n• **Back Strain**: On December 21, 2024, Taylor presented with complaints of back strain, likely due to a recent physical activity. A thorough examination revealed no other musculoskeletal issues. She was advised to perform gentle stretching exercises and apply ice to the affected area. Over-the-counter pain relievers were recommended as needed.\n\n• **Vital Signs**: At the most recent visit, Taylor's blood pressure was 127/87 mmHg, and her weight was 142 lbs. These findings are within normal limits and consistent with her age and height.\n\n• **Exercise**: Taylor maintains an active lifestyle and engages in running 3-4 times a week. This consistent physical activity has been beneficial for her overall health and well-being.\n\n• **Social History**: \n - **Tobacco Use**: Taylor has a history of tobacco use, specifically cigarettes, starting in May 2014. She smoked approximately 1.5 packs per day until she quit in June 2015. Taylor has been honest and compliant with her disclosure regarding her former tobacco use.\n - **Alcohol Use**: Taylor consumes alcohol regularly, with an intake of about 10 drinks per week. This is within the moderate range and has not led to any significant health concerns.\n\n• **Family History**: Taylor's father has a history of coronary artery disease (CAD) that began at age 59. He is currently living and being managed for his condition. This family history underscores the importance of monitoring cardiovascular health in Taylor.\n\n• **Additional Findings**: During the course of her visits, Taylor has had normal findings on her physical examinations, including normal heart sounds, clear lung fields, and no signs of distress. She reports occasional minor complaints, such as headaches and fatigue, which are not associated with any significant underlying condition.\n\n• **Medications**: Taylor is currently taking guanfacine 1 mg daily for her ADHD. This medication has been effect"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ive in managing her symptoms and is well-tolerated. There have been no reported side effects.\n\n• **Preventive Care**: Taylor has been advised to continue her regular follow-ups to monitor her ADHD and overall health. Vaccinations are up-to-date, and has received appropriate screenings for her age.\n\nThis summary reflects Taylor Mata's medical history, including her management of ADHD and recent episode of back strain. Her current health status is stable, and she is compliant with her treatment plan. Her lifestyle choices, including regular exercise and moderate alcohol consumption, contribute positively to her overall health.\n"
    }
